**script.js:**
```javascript
const loginForm = document.getElementById('login-form');

loginForm.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();

    const username = document.getElementById('username').value.trim();
    const password = document.getElementById('password').value.trim();

    if (username === '' || password === '') {
        alert('Please enter both username and password');
    } else {
        console.log(`Username: ${username}, Password: ${password}`);
    }
});
```

This code creates a simple login form with a username and password field. When the user submits the form, it checks if both fields are filled and logs the input values to the console. You can modify this code to suit your specific requirements.

